.nh
.TH "PB-ENV-RUN" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-run - Run a command with your workspace ENV in its environment


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env run -- <command> [args...] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a command with the ENV of the active workspace merged into its environment, for scripts and CI where no shell hook is installed. Values go straight to the child process: never to disk, logs or its arguments. Stdin, stdout, stderr, signals and the exit code pass through. If the ENV cannot be loaded, the command does not run.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for run


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb env run -- npm test
  pb env run --workspace my-team -- ./deploy.sh --prod
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env(1)\fP
